========================================================================
(A) CHARACTER-TRIVIALITY:  F(rho) = (p-1)^c  exactly, for every even cactus
    (c = #blocks = cycle rank).  If true => leading coeff is pure Moebius.
   k=2: checked 3 even cacti, F=(p-1)^c for ALL p,rho:  True
   k=3: checked 12 even cacti, F=(p-1)^c for ALL p,rho:  True
========================================================================
(B) PURE MOEBIUS IDENTITY   S_k = sum_{even cacti} mu(0,rho)  =?  (-1)^k C_k
    (no primes, no characters -- pure partition lattice)
     k      S_k   (-1)^k C_k   match   #even-cacti
     1       -1           -1    True   1
        profile -> mu-sum: (2,):-1
     2        2            2    True   3
        profile -> mu-sum: (4,):-1  (2, 2):+3
     3       -6           -5   False   12
        profile -> mu-sum: (6,):-1  (2, 4):+8  (2, 2, 2):-13
     4       25           14   False   55
        profile -> mu-sum: (8,):-1  (2, 6):+10  (4, 4):+5  (2, 2, 4):-58  (2, 2, 2, 2):+69
     5     -132          -42   False   273
        profile -> mu-sum: (10,):-1  (2, 8):+12  (4, 6):+12  (2, 2, 6):-81  (2, 4, 4):-81  (2, 2, 2, 4):+428  (2, 2, 2, 2, 2):-421
========================================================================
(C) bigon-tree-ONLY |mu|-sum (all blocks = bigons) = OEIS A088368 (~e*n!)
    vs Catalan after the even-cycle-cactus corrections
    k:               1      2      3      4      5      6
    A088368:         1      3     13     69    421   2867
    Catalan C_k:     1      2      5     14     42    132
========================================================================
CONCLUSION: the Catalan leading coefficient is a PURE partition-lattice
Moebius sum over even-cactus gluings of the path -- the character content
collapses to F(rho)=(p-1)^c.  Handoff #1 reduces to the number-theory-FREE
identity  ($) sum_{even cacti}(-1)^c prod(|B|-1)! = (-1)^k C_k,  the
moment->free-cumulant (semicircle) relation; Wigner-universal (HYP-2308).
